    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a"/><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief a cuntę, ki al rei afert: VIII chevals, enfrenez e enseelez . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.b"/>, e IIII haubercs e IIII haumes e IIII escuz e IIII lances e IIII espees. Les autres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.c"/>: II chaceurs e II palefreis a freins e a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.1"/><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.2"/> al cunte, que al rei afiert: VIII chivals<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.3"/>, selez e enfrenez les<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.4"/> IIII, . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a-2"/> halbers e IIII haumes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.5"/> e IIII escuz e IIII launces e IIII espés. Les altres IIII: chaceurs e palefreiz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.6"/> a freins<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.7"/> et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.8"/> a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De releuiis. Releuium comitis, quod ad regem pertinet: VIII equi, ex quibus IIII erunt sellati et frenati, et cum eis IIII lorice, IIII galee, IIII lancee, IIII scuta et IIII gladii. Alii IIII equi erunt palefridi et chascuri cum freinis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.1-2"/> et camis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a-3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="20" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="262" ed="#robertson"/>De relief a cunte ki al rei afert: VIII chevals, enfrenez e enseelez [les IIII], e IIII haubercs e IIII haumes e IIII escuz e IIII lances e IIII espees. Les autres [IIII]: II chaceurs e II palefreis a freins e a chevestres.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>20. An Heergeräthe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.de.1"/> für einen [verstorbenen] Grafen, welches dem König zukommt: 8 Pferde, (davon <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) gezäumt und gesattelt 4, und 4 Panzerhemden und 4 Helme und 4 Schilde und 4 Lanzen und 4 Schwerter. Die anderen 4 (Pferde <hi rend="italic">L</hi>): 2 Jagdpferde und 2 Zelter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_20.lnote.de1.a"/> mit Zäumen und mit Halftern.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">20. As heriot for a [deceased] count, which falls to the king: 8 horses, (of them <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) bridled and saddled 4, and 4 coats of mail and 4 helmets and 4 shields and 4 lances and 4 swords. The other 4 (horses <hi rend="italic">L</hi>): 2 hunting horses and 2 palfreys with bridles and with halters.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="263" ed="#robertson"/>The heriot of an earl, which falls to the King, is 8 horses—4 of them bridled and saddled—4 coats of mail, 4 helmets, 4 shields, 4 lances and 4 swords. Of the other 4 horses, 2 shall be hunters and 2 riding horses with bridles and halters.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="507"><ref target="clause:IICn_71a">II Cn 71a</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 71a</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>loosely based on</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_70">II Cn 70–71</ref> <quote>passages loosely based on Cnut's laws about ... heriots</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); 20–20.3a come after 28.2 in Hk; Robertson follows the order of I and L, as other editors do.; Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 506–507, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">20—20, 3a <hi rend="italic">setzt hinter</hi> 28, 2 <hi rend="italic">Hk; Edd. ordnen gemäss IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hk places 20—20, 3a after 28, 2; edd. arrange according to IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> les IIII <hi rend="italic">aus IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply les IIII from IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> IIII <hi rend="italic">aus IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply IIII from IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a-2" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> e IIII <hi rend="italic">aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply e IIII from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">releife <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">releife <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">chivalz <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">chivalz <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lez <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lez <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hammes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hammes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">palfreis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">palfreis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">frenis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">frenis <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.a-3" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in Vulgata</hi> camus: <hi rend="italic">Zügelgebiss des Pferdes und Esels</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the Vulgate camus: the bit of the bridle of horse and ass</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Reisepferde</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">travelling horses</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_20.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Heergewäte 2. a. b. 11b. 12. a. Steenstrup hält die Abweichungen von Cnut für absichtslose Fehler. Unmöglich scheint Ramsays Annahme (<hi rend="italic">Foundat. of Engl</hi>. II 141, hieraus und aus Hn 14), das alte Heergewäte bestehe <hi rend="spaced">neben</hi> dem Relevium fort (was fürs bäuerliche <hi rend="italic">heriot</hi> [<hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 20, 3{1}] allerdings gilt); denn dann hätte man nicht jenes durch dieses übersetzt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Heergewäte 2. a. b. 11b. 12. a. Steenstrup regards the deviations from Cnut as unintentional errors. Ramsay’s assumption (<hi rend="italic">Foundat. of Engl</hi>. II 141, from this and from Hn 14) that the old heriot continued to exist <hi rend="italic">alongside</hi> the relevium (which does indeed hold for the peasant’s <hi rend="italic">heriot</hi> [<hi rend="italic">below</hi> 20, 3{1}]) seems impossible; for in that case the former would not have been translated by the latter</seg></note>
      </div>
